## Mechanism (read at upstream/main d99fc204)

`forceDelete` -> `stopJob`: normal stop fails (the stop action resolves the id and fails with a resource-not-found for an absent config), then a force stop is attempted and fails the same way. The failure handler then does:

    logger.error(() -> "[" + id + "] Failed to stop normally", normalStopFailure);
    logger.error(() -> "[" + id + "] Failed to stop forcefully", forceStopFailure);
    listener.onFailure(forceStopFailure);

The non-force path (`normalDelete`) fails the same missing id through `configProvider.get` and logs nothing. So a client 404 on `DELETE _ml/data_frame/analytics/<id>?force=true` yields 2 ERRORs with stacks, while the same request without `force` is silent. The caller receives the 404 either way.

Proof level: code read; stop-action 404 path read by name (`ResourceNotFoundException` import/ExpandedIdsMatcher), not executed.

## Proposal

Skip the two ERROR lines when the unwrapped cause is `ResourceNotFoundException` (propagate to listener only), or log them at DEBUG. Keep ERROR for other stop failures.

